==Bislama==

===Etymology===
Cognate to {{cog|tpi|bensin||petrol}}. According to Terry Crowley, this term entered {{etyl|bi|-}} pre-1885, either from {{etyl|de|bi}} {{m|de|Benzin}}, or from {{etyl|en|bi}} {{m|en|benzene}}, as the meaning of that term was not as narrow or technical in the nineteenth century as it is today.<ref>Terry Crowley, ''Beach-la-Mar to Bislama: the emergence of a national language in Vanuatu'' (1990), page 137.</ref>

===Noun===
{{head|bi|noun}}

# [[gasoline]], [[petrol]]

